opening='The “meaning from the West” is the shortened public-interview form of the question about the patriarch’s coming from the West; the records answer it with fresh words and actions rather than one explanatory definition.'
body='Direct abbreviated questions ask simply “what is the meaning from the West?” Tianzhu Chonghui answers with a white ape carrying its young and butterflies holding flowers; Helin Xuansu answers that understanding is not understanding and doubt is not doubt. Yunfeng Zudeng answers with striking the forehead and nose, Mazu Daoyi asks what meaning is present now, Sanfeng Hanyue Fazang says “three years carrying one boat,” Linji asks Longya for the Chan board, Zhaozhou descends from the seat, and Shitou sends the questioner to ask the exposed pillar. The Chan bend is the abbreviation’s life as a public test whose many incompatible replies are preserved rather than harmonized into a hidden proposition.'
